      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start with the polynomial equation:\n\n\\[\nx^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\) are the roots of this polynomial, we can use Vieta's formulas to find the relationships between the roots and the coefficients of the polynomial. Vieta's formulas tell us:\n\n1. \\( r + s + t = 5 \\)\n2. \\( rs + rt + st = 6 \\)\n3. \\( rst = 9 \\)\n\nWe need to compute the value of:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's express each term in the given expression in terms of \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} = \\frac{rs}{t} = \\frac{rs}{t}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{st}{r} = \\frac{st}{r} = \\frac{st}{r}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{tr}{s}\n\\]\n\nCombining these, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\n\\]\n\nNotice that we can rewrite each fraction with a common denominator involving \\( rst \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} = \\frac{rs}{t} \\cdot \\frac{st}{st} = \\frac{(rs)st}{t \\cdot st} = \\frac{rs \\cdot st}{rst \\cdot t} = \\frac{rs \\cdot st}{9t}\n\\]\n\nSimilarly,\n\n\\[\n\\frac{st}{r} = \\frac{st}{r} \\cdot \\frac{rt}{rt} = \\frac{st \\cdot rt}{r \\cdot rt} = \\frac{st \\cdot rt}{rst \\cdot r} = \\frac{st \\cdot rt}{9r}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{tr}{s} \\cdot \\frac{st}{st} = \\frac{tr \\cdot st}{s \\cdot st} = \\frac{tr \\cdot st}{rst \\cdot s} = \\frac{tr \\cdot st}{9s}\n\\]\n\nNow, summing these fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot st}{9t} + \\frac{st \\cdot rt}{9r} + \\frac{tr \\cdot st}{9s}\n\\]\n\nFactoring out the common term \\( \\frac{rst}{9} \\):\n\n\\[\n= \\frac{rst}{9} \\left( \\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} \\right)\n\\]\n\nWe recognize that the expression inside the parentheses is precisely the sum of the elements taken two at a time according to Vieta's formulas:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = 6\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rst}{9} \\cdot 6 = \\frac{6rst}{9}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( rst = 9 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6 \\cdot 9}{9} = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
