      "text": "The given cubic equation is \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\). Let \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) be the roots of this equation. By Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9.\n\\]\n\nWe need to compute the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). We can rewrite this expression in terms of the roots \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rs + st \\cdot st + tr \\cdot tr}{rst} = \\frac{r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2}{rst}.\n\\]\n\nWe can express \\(r^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2\\) in terms of \\(rs + rt + st\\) and \\(rst\\):\n\\[\nr^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2 = (rs + rt + st)^2 - 2rst(r + s + t).\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\) and \\(rst = 9\\) and \\(r + s + t = 5\\), we get:\n\\[\nr^2s^2 + s^2t^2 + t^2r^2 = 6^2 - 2 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 36 - 90 = -54.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{-54}{9} = -6.\n\\]\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-6}.\n\\]",
